# DXF Viewport Analyzer

Automated analysis of paper-space viewports in DXF drawings.

DXF Viewport Analyzer inspects layouts, detects viewport configurations, extracts viewport properties, maps viewport content, and generates reports for CAD quality control workflows.

## Features

✅ Detect paper-space layouts

✅ Detect and enumerate viewports

✅ Extract viewport properties
- Center point
- Width and height
- Scale
- View center
- View target
- Twist angle
- Lock status

✅ Analyze viewport geometry

✅ Determine model-space entities visible through each viewport

✅ Generate viewport inventories

✅ Export results as JSON

✅ Support automated QC workflows

## Example Output

```json
{
  "layout": "Sheet 1",
  "viewport_count": 2,
  "viewports": [
    {
      "viewport_id": 1,
      "scale": "1:100",
      "locked": true,
      "visible_entities": 245
    },
    {
      "viewport_id": 2,
      "scale": "1:50",
      "locked": true,
      "visible_entities": 83
    }
  ]
}

Why This Project?

Most DXF tools focus on geometry inside model space.

This project focuses on what users actually see on plotted sheets:

Layouts
Viewports
Scales
Visible content
Sheet composition

This enables automated CAD quality control and sheet validation.

Use Cases
Survey Drawing Validation

Verify:

Required information appears on sheets
Viewports are correctly scaled
Viewports are locked
Expected entities are visible
CAD Quality Control

Identify:

Missing viewports
Empty viewports
Incorrect scales
Viewports showing unintended content
Automated Reporting

Generate viewport reports for:

Survey drawings
Plat maps
Civil engineering plans
Construction drawings
Architecture
